From 7b84b123277c96c1bc7d3f5e4613e66d2c67322d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:29:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] Add an optional per-run cost guard

agent.MAX_RUN_COST_USD (off unless set; no checked-in profile sets it)
ends a run with the new exit reason COST_CAP once its estimated spend
exceeds the limit.

- The estimate is the run's recorded usage (accepted and retried action
  attempts plus harness summaries) at the configured per-million pricing,
  with no cache or service-tier discount, matching how ARC reconstructs
  published costs. Under a discounted tier it overstates the bill.
- is_done checks it before each action, after GAME_WIN and the per-level
  action budget, so those endings take precedence. The action whose
  request crossed the limit is still executed; overshoot is at most one
  step's requests.
- run_meta.json records cost_guard {max_usd, estimated_cost_usd} when the
  guard is on and omits it otherwise.
- Config validation requires a positive number and numeric
  pricing.input/pricing.output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
