+## Cost guard
+
+`agent.MAX_RUN_COST_USD` is an optional per-run spend limit; it is off unless a
+configuration sets it, and none of the checked-in profiles does. The estimate
+is the run's recorded usage (accepted and retried action attempts plus harness
+summaries) at the configured `pricing` per million input and output tokens.
+Like ARC's published costs, it applies no cache or service-tier discount, so
+under a discounted tier it overstates the bill. Before each action the agent
+compares the estimate with the limit; once it exceeds the limit, the run ends
+with exit reason `COST_CAP`. The action whose request crossed the limit has
+already been paid for and is executed first, so a run can overshoot by one
+step's requests. A win or an exhausted action budget at the same point takes
+precedence. `run_meta.json` records `cost_guard` with the limit and the current
+estimate; the field is omitted when the guard is off.
+
 ## Recording and provenance
 
 ### xAI Responses
